From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: clear latched FEC detection before Uke link training

FEC detected flags are receiver events, not a live decoder-enable state.
Clear both write-one-to-clear flags after FEC_READY, as upstream's DP sink
preparation does, so a reconnect cannot accept an earlier enable event.
Propagate a failed clear before link training or DSC admission. Preserve
uncompressed and PHY-test paths.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
@@ -1795,6 +1795,11 @@ static int msm_dp_ctrl_setup_main_link(struct msm_dp_ctrl_private *ctrl,
 		ret = drm_dp_dpcd_write_byte(ctrl->aux, DP_FEC_CONFIGURATION, DP_FEC_READY);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
+		/* Detection flags are latched; require a fresh enable event. */
+		ret = drm_dp_dpcd_write_byte(ctrl->aux, DP_FEC_STATUS,
+				DP_FEC_DECODE_EN_DETECTED | DP_FEC_DECODE_DIS_DETECTED);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
 	}
 
 	/*
